Level 4: File Manipulation

Mission: Create a script that copies all .txt files from the Arena directory to a new directory called Backup.

We have to run through the Arena directory, search for all files that end in .txt and then copy them to a new directory called backup.
The backup directory has to live outside the Arena directory (if the Arena directory gets affected it won't affect the backups)

bench:~/DevOps/BattleBashArena/Arena# touch Backup.sh
bench:~/DevOps/BattleBashArena/Arena# vi Backup.sh

we will have to use a loop to go through each file, we can use a for loop with the amount of files in a directory as the number to reach for amount of loops.
This is safer than a while loop which could cause an endless loop.
When we check each file we would have an if statement which would check if it ends in .txt.

Lets go line by line explaining design choices.

List=($(ls -a)) 
The ls -a command will show a list of files in a directory including the hidden ones, we put these in brackets to create an array of the different files that show up.
If we created the List like this List=$(ls -a) it would treat the whole output as 1 string and would not let us select each file independantly. 
